      "message": "Do I need to do something about these KMI warnings?\n\n```\n\u0027struct fscrypt_info at fscrypt_private.h:195:1\u0027 changed:\n  type size hasn\u0027t changed\n  there are data member changes:\n    type \u0027key*\u0027 of \u0027fscrypt_info::ci_master_key\u0027 changed:\n      pointer type changed from: \u0027key*\u0027 to: \u0027fscrypt_master_key*\u0027\n  2741 impacted interfaces\n\n\u0027struct super_block at fs.h:1450:1\u0027 changed:\n  type size hasn\u0027t changed\n  there are data member changes:\n    type \u0027key*\u0027 of \u0027super_block::s_master_keys\u0027 changed:\n      pointer type changed from: \u0027key*\u0027 to: \u0027fscrypt_keyring*\u0027\n  2741 impacted interfaces\n```\n\n`struct fscrypt_info` isn\u0027t supposed to be part of the KMI at all, as it\u0027s only used internally by built-in code in `fs/crypto/`.  We had discussed this last year, and I was told it had been fixed.  Apparently not.\n\n`struct super_block` as a whole is part of the KMI, I guess, but the specific field being changed here is likewise only for use by built-in code in `fs/crypto/`.\n\nSo I believe these changes are perfectly safe to make; it is just the ABI tooling that is complaining.",
